2. There exist  $ n$  real numbers  $ x_i$ , linearly independent over  $ \mathbb{Q}$  (take them from a Hamel basis);
3. The sets  $ D_i \equal{} (x_i, x_i) \plus{} D$  are disjoint, and each still dense in  $ \mathbb{R}^2$ ;
4. Color  $ D_i$  using color  $ C_i$ , and the rest of the points of the plane (randomly) at will.

So why all the fuss?

