    \angle P^*Q^*O+\angle OQ^*E^*&=\angle P^*CO+\angle QCE^*=\angle PCO=90^\circ
\end{align*}
Means  $\angle P^*Q^*E^*$  is right angle and  $P^*E^*$  is the diameter of  $\triangle P^*Q^*E^*$ . Similarly  $\angle P^*R^*E^*=90^\circ$ . So  $P^*Q^*E^*R^*$  is cyclic. The line  $BD$  is tangent to the cyclic quadrilateral  $P^*Q^*E^*R^*$  at  $E^*$ . So the cyclic quadrilateral  $PQER$  is tangent to  $(BOD)$  at  $E$ .

