We call a permutation of the set of real numbers  $\{a_1,\cdots,a_n\}$ ,  $n\in\mathbb{N}$  *average increasing* if the arithmetic mean of its first  $k$  elements for  $k=1,\cdots ,n$  form a strictly increasing sequence. 

