We are given:   $$ -x^2y^2z^2+xyz+1-xy-yz-zx=0. $$  Therefore,
\begin{align*}
\frac{x(1-yz)+y(1-xz)+z(1-xy)}{(1-xy)(1-yz)(1-zx)}&=\frac{-3xyz}{(1-xy)(1-yz)(1-zx)}&=\frac{-3xyz}{-x^2y^2z^2+xy^2z+xyz^2+x^2yz-xy-yz-zx+1}&=\frac{-3xyz}{xy^2z+xyz^2+x^2yz-xyz}&=\frac{-3}{y+x+z-1}=3.
\end{align*}

